<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felek al-Din Dundar Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1324</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felek al-Din Dundar Bey was the founder of the Hamidid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in the Lakes Region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, a grandson of Hamid Bey, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>. As Seljuk power collapsed in the early 14th century he made himself ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egirdir">Eğirdir</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isparta">Isparta</a>. He was executed in 1324 by the Ilkhanid governor Timurtash.</p></div>
